  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1901.12 “Floor plan” means a form of third party financing used by car dealerships for the financing of the dealership’s inventory of vehicles displayed for sale, in which the vehicles serve as collateral for the financing.\n\nSource. #13614, eff 4-25-23",
